{"id":"mahabharata-5-108","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":108,"title":"अष्टाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 108 · Garuda describes the west","summary":{"en":"Garuda describes the western quarter, beloved of Varuna, lord of the waters, where the sun sets and the golden mountain stands by the ocean shore.","kn":"ಜಲಾಧಿಪತಿ ವರುಣನಿಗೆ ಪ್ರಿಯವಾದ, ಸೂರ್ಯನು ಅಸ್ತಮಿಸುವ, ಸಮುದ್ರತೀರದಲ್ಲಿ ಸುವರ್ಣಪರ್ವತವಿರುವ ಪಶ್ಚಿಮದಿಕ್ಕನ್ನು ಗರುಡನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"गरुड़ पश्चिम दिशा का वर्णन करते हैं, जो जल के स्वामी वरुण को प्रिय है, जहाँ सूर्य अस्त होता है और समुद्र-तट पर स्वर्ण पर्वत खड़ा है।","te":"జలాధిపతి వరుణునికి ప్రియమైన, సూర్యుడు అస్తమించే, సముద్రతీరంలో బంగారు పర్వతం ఉన్న పశ్చిమ దిక్కును గరుడుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"நீரின் இறைவன் வருணனுக்குப் பிரியமான, சூரியன் மறையும், கடற்கரையில் பொன்மலை நிற்கும் மேற்குத் திசையைக் கருடன் விவரிக்கிறான்.","ml":"ജലാധിപനായ വരുണന് പ്രിയപ്പെട്ട പടിഞ്ഞാറൻ ദിക്ക് ഗരുഡൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; അവിടെ സൂര്യൻ അസ്തമിക്കുന്നു, സമുദ്രതീരത്ത് സ്വർണ്ണപർവ്വതം നിൽക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.108; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"सुपर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suparna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इयं दिग्दयिता राज्ञो वरुणस्य तु गोपतेः ।\nसदा सलिलराजस्य प्रतिष्ठा चादिरेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"This direction is dear to King Varuna, lord of the waters and protector of cattle, and it is always the foundation and origin of the king of waters."}},{"n":2,"text":"अत्र पश्चादहः सूर्यो विसर्जयति भाः स्वयम् ।\nपश्चिमेत्यभिविख्याता दिगियं द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the sun at the close of day lets go of his own light; so this direction, best of brahmins, is famed as the western."}},{"n":3,"text":"यादसामत्र राज्येन सलिलस्य च गुप्तये ।\nकश्यपो भगवान्देवो वरुणं स्माभ्यषेचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the blessed divine Kashyapa anointed Varuna to rule the water creatures and to guard the waters."}},{"n":4,"text":"अत्र पीत्वा समस्तान्वै वरुणस्य रसांस्तु षट् ।\nजायते तरुणः सोमः शुक्लस्यादौ तमिस्रहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the young moon, which drives away darkness, drinks all six flavors of Varuna and is born at the start of the bright fortnight."}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्र पश्चात्कृता दैत्या वायुना संयतास्तदा ।\nनिःश्वसन्तो महानागैरर्दिताः सुषुपुर्द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the Daityas, driven behind by Vayu and bound, afflicted by great serpents, lay sighing and fell asleep, brahmin."}},{"n":6,"text":"अत्र सूर्यं प्रणयिनं प्रतिगृह्णाति पर्वतः ।\nअस्तो नाम यतः संध्या पश्चिमा प्रतिसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the mountain named Asta receives the beloved sun, from which the western twilight creeps forward."}},{"n":7,"text":"अतो रात्रिश्च निद्रा च निर्गता दिवसक्षये ।\nजायते जीवलोकस्य हर्तुमर्धमिवायुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From it, at the day's end, night and sleep come out and spread over the living world as if to take away half its life."}},{"n":8,"text":"अत्र देवीं दितिं सुप्तामात्मप्रसवधारिणीम् ।\nविगर्भामकरोच्छक्रो यत्र जातो मरुद्गणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here Indra made the goddess Diti, who was asleep bearing her own offspring, miscarry; from this the troop of Maruts was born."}},{"n":9,"text":"अत्र मूलं हिमवतो मन्दरं याति शाश्वतम् ।\nअपि वर्षसहस्रेण न चास्यान्तोऽधिगम्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the eternal root of the Himalaya reaches Mandara; even in a thousand years its end cannot be found."}},{"n":10,"text":"अत्र काञ्चनशैलस्य काञ्चनाम्बुवहस्य च ।\nउदधेस्तीरमासाद्य सुरभिः क्षरते पयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here, reaching the shore of the sea beside the golden mountain that carries golden waters, Surabhi pours out her milk."}},{"n":11,"text":"अत्र मध्ये समुद्रस्य कबन्धः प्रतिदृश्यते ।\nस्वर्भानोः सूर्यकल्पस्य सोमसूर्यौ जिघांसतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here in the middle of the ocean is seen the headless trunk of Svarbhanu, sun-like, who tried to kill the moon and the sun."}},{"n":12,"text":"सुवर्णशिरसोऽप्यत्र हरिरोम्णः प्रगायतः ।\nअदृश्यस्याप्रमेयस्य श्रूयते विपुलो ध्वनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here too a vast sound is heard of the unseen and immeasurable golden-headed, tawny-haired singer."}},{"n":13,"text":"अत्र ध्वजवती नाम कुमारी हरिमेधसः ।\nआकाशे तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति तस्थौ सूर्यस्य शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the maiden Dhvajavati, daughter of Harimedhas, stayed in the sky at the sun's command, when he said 'Stay, stay.'"}},{"n":14,"text":"अत्र वायुस्तथा वह्निरापः खं चैव गालव ।\nआह्निकं चैव नैशं च दुःखस्पर्शं विमुञ्चति ।\nअतः प्रभृति सूर्यस्य तिर्यगावर्तते गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here wind, fire, water and sky, Galava, release the painful touch of day and night. From here on the sun's course turns aslant."}},{"n":15,"text":"अत्र ज्योतींषि सर्वाणि विशन्त्यादित्यमण्डलम् ।\nअष्टाविंशतिरात्रं च चङ्क्रम्य सह भानुना ।\nनिष्पतन्ति पुनः सूर्यात्सोमसंयोगयोगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here all the luminaries enter the sun's disk, and after travelling for twenty-eight nights with the sun, they leave the sun again through union with the moon."}},{"n":16,"text":"अत्र नित्यं स्रवन्तीनां प्रभवः सागरोदयः ।\nअत्र लोकत्रयस्यापस्तिष्ठन्ति वरुणाश्रयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here is always the source of rivers and the rising of the sea; here the waters of the three worlds stand, resting on Varuna."}},{"n":17,"text":"अत्र पन्नगराजस्याप्यनन्तस्य निवेशनम् ।\nअनादिनिधनस्यात्र विष्णोः स्थानमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here is the dwelling of Ananta, king of serpents, and here is the supreme place of Vishnu, without beginning or end."}},{"n":18,"text":"अत्रानलसखस्यापि पवनस्य निवेशनम् ।\nमहर्षेः कश्यपस्यात्र मारीचस्य निवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here is the dwelling of the wind, friend of fire, and here is the dwelling of the great sage Kashyapa, son of Marichi."}},{"n":19,"text":"एष ते पश्चिमो मार्गो दिग्द्वारेण प्रकीर्तितः ।\nब्रूहि गालव गच्छावो बुद्धिः का द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the western road, named by the gateway of its direction. Tell me, Galava, where do we go? What is your mind, best of brahmins?"}}]}]}